From 05f588bd37dafd9d8fb9dd1dcc16069d2ecc88bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] fix: end-of-phase-2 polish batch (B-36, B-38, B-39,
 B-40)

The plan routed these to a "polish" batch at the end of Phase 2 and they
were skipped; the self-review picked them up.

- B-36 POST /api/chat/voice runs the media quota check synchronously and
  answers media_pending=false + media_error when the recording will not be
  kept, instead of media_pending=true for a background store that then
  failed silently. The UI shows that message; transcript delivery unchanged.
- B-38 Browser speech recognition joins consecutive sessions with a space
  ("...done Now..." instead of "...doneNow...") both while previewing and
  when committing.
- B-39 User docs: voice language is Auto-detect / English / Persian and
  there is no "refine step"; admin docs no longer list "voice refinement";
  modelCatalog.ts drops the never-emitted is_transcription_default in favour
  of default_kinds, which the API actually sends.
- B-40 .env.example had COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME twice; the app's /tmp tmpfs
  was 10 GiB of RAM for ZIP packs whose default ceiling is 256 MiB - now 2g
  with the sizing rule in the comment. sync_edge_body_limit compares both
  ceilings (upload and JSON) before deciding nginx.conf is unchanged, so a
  MAX_JSON_BODY_BYTES change reaches the edge without an upload-ceiling
  change; the per-worker generation bump only happens when the file really
  differs.

